Zs6-gDUj","user":{"login":"vladmoroz","id":8441036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDEwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8441036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz","html_url":"https://github.com/vladmoroz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladmoroz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T10:22:50Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T10:27:50Z","body":"Will `event.preventBaseUIHandler()` remove Base UI side effects like this Esc propagation stopped?\r\nhttps://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/589511b4bf0836e01fd7706973469a12039abc51/packages/react/src/floating-ui-react/hooks/useDismiss.ts#L192\r\n\r\nMy problem / use case:\r\n\r\nI've got a non-modal dialog which I'd like it to close on Esc only if an element in the dialog is focused, otherwise keep the dialog open and use Esc in my own handler.\r\n\r\nIt's easy to keep the dialog open after Esc keypress, but I can't process Esc on my side because dialogs swallow Esc and it doesn't reach my event listener\r\n\r\n(I have to say in most cases it's very appreciated that dialogs stop Esc propagation when I do want them to close the way it works by default, but when I want to prevent the default behavior, I want complete control over everything)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comm